@tradition five-minute-skills
// Round 2: each time Bilal Nakamura brings a crewmate to teach one small thing in five minutes, then everyone tries. Even weeks from week 2.
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
k: 1301
title: Five-minute skills
when: every 2 weeks monday week 2
at: 18:15-18:45
min: 20
after-shift: yes
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
who: nakamura-bilal always, watch 30%, juniors 30%, everyone 10%
anim: nakamura-bilal talk, everyone fold
host: nakamura-bilal
from: nakamura-bilal
invite: host=nakamura-bilal odds=25% line="Five-minute skills, the bow lounge. Someone teaches one thing. You learn it. That's all."

== mail
- Five-minute skills tomorrow, {time}, the bow lounge. One crewmate, one small skill, five minutes. Then everyone tries. This time's is a surprise.

== ask
- Five-minute skills in the bow lounge. Last time was tying a bowline.
- Bilal's got someone teaching how to fold a fitted sheet. Nobody can.   #funny
- Learn one thing in five minutes? I can manage that. Just.

== here
- Over, under, through. Pull. There.
- Watch the hands, not the face.
- Again. Slower this time. Good.
- That's a skill now. Yours.   #warm

== thanks
- A crewmate teaches one small skill in five minutes, Bilal keeps time, and then everyone has a go. You leave knowing one more thing.   #warm

== chatter
- I can splice a cable now. Bilal timed it. Six minutes, but still.
- Five-minute skills. I finally folded a fitted sheet. It took eleven.   #funny
- Bilal says everyone aboard knows one thing worth teaching. He's working through the list.
